{
  "about": "Test vectors for the chained commitment over every subject's log that a bureau keeping one log per subject publishes (Agent Reputations §4.1.1). The tree is a sparse Merkle tree of height 256: each subject has one slot, at the SHA-256 of its name lowercased; a slot holds the subject's head or the tombstone of an erased subject, and its digest is SHA-256 over the byte 0x00 and the JCS of what it holds; an empty subtree of height h has the digest EMPTY[h], 32 zero bytes at height 0 and SHA-256 over 0x01 and two copies of EMPTY[h-1] above; a node is SHA-256 over 0x01, its left child and its right child; bit 0 of a key, the highest bit of its first byte, chooses the side at the root. A proof lists the sibling of each level from the slot up, null for an empty subtree. Commitments are signed under the tag fdbk-heads-v1 with the report test key of fdbk-report-v1.json, and each names the previous one in prev: SHA-256 over its signed bytes. reference.mjs beside this file reproduces every vector.",
